<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    skin.daylight palettes (AARRGGBB). Four moods x the same token set:
      m_ = Morning 06-11 (pale sky)   a_ = Afternoon 11-17 (bright, warm neutral)
      e_ = Evening 17-22 (warm dusk)  n_ = Night 22-06 (deep blue, dimmer, lower contrast, still >= 4.5:1)
    Windows NEVER use these names directly: every colour goes through a mood token variable
    ($VAR[DL_Ink], $VAR[DL_Accent] ...) defined in 1080i/Includes_Daylight.xml (generated by
    _src/make_time_vars.py), which picks the palette by System.Time or the forced mood setting.
    Source of truth for the values: docs/skin.daylight/DESIGN.md (from the concept mockups).
-->
